# Gemma 4 12B generation environment (generate.py: vLLM sampling + SENTINEL's tools). vLLM 0.30.0 is the first release
# that requires transformers >= 5.10.4 (the Gemma 4 era) and it sets no upper bound, so it runs with transformers 5.20.2,
# the version of the probe paper's Gemma-4-12B environment (policy.lock.txt). vLLM 0.31 and 0.32 cap transformers below
# 5.18 / 5.20, and 0.33 needs torch 2.14, built only for CUDA 13. vLLM 0.30 needs torch 2.13, built for CUDA 12.9 (NVIDIA
# driver >= 570 via CUDA minor-version compatibility): this venv is installed with --torch-backend cu129 (gen.torch-backend). The tools are pinned as in
# ../../requirements.txt.
# vLLM's PyPI wheel is built for CUDA 13 (needs NVIDIA driver >= 580); its CUDA 12.9 build comes from vLLM's own index
# and runs on drivers >= 570 (CUDA minor-version compatibility), like the torch 2.13 cu129 build next to it.
--extra-index-url https://wheels.vllm.ai/0.30.0/cu129
vllm==0.30.0+cu129
transformers==5.20.2
tokenizers==0.23.3
